# Important NVRAM / Bootflash Issue Observed

During the recovery process, this ISR 4321 displayed:

    % Failed to initialize nvram
    % Failed to initialize backup nvram

It also displayed:

    %Error opening bootflash:/nvram (No such file or directory)

At one point, the router also displayed:

    Failed to find bootable image on device bootflash:
    autoboot: boot failed, restarting...

However, the IOS image was successfully found in bootflash:

    isr4300-universalk9.16.08.01.SPA.bin

Therefore:

- Do not delete the IOS image.
- Do not format `bootflash:`.
- Do not format NVRAM.
- Do not randomly delete bootflash files.
- If `erase startup-config` reports an NVRAM/storage error, stop and investigate the storage issue first.

